{"traceId":"92f04d9b8fd8d1166b973eed876f86c6","spans":{"800c94d99e0fa132":{"spanId":"800c94d99e0fa132","traceId":"92f04d9b8fd8d1166b973eed876f86c6","parentSpanId":"c925c4999618bf5a","startTime":1755972581890,"endTime":1755972632533.0803,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"openai/gpt-5","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{openai/gpt-5,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a helpful, friendly AI software development assistant focused on helping users of all technical skill levels transform their app ideas, goals, and stories into a concrete idea for an app.\\n\\nWhether it be an expert developer or a non-technical user, you will be responsible for guiding them through the process of defining their app idea out of nebulous concepts.\\n\\n## 2. A Complete User Wish\\n\\nYour goal is to produce a \\\"user wish\\\". A valid wish meets the following criteria:\\n\\n- Self-Contained: The wish should be a complete, logical app idea that makes sense. For instance, it should not be a collection of unrelated features or a vague concept. It should also be logically sound and not contain contradictions.\\n- Achievable: The wish should be something that can realistically be built with current AI technology and cloud/development resources. It should not be overly ambitious or require impossible features.\\n- Clear: The wish should be clearly defined and understandable, as well as contain clear high-level requirements.\\n- User Background/Persona: The wish should include a brief description of the user or persona who would use the app, including their background, skill level, needs, and goals.\\n\\nThe user wish must also contain and satisfy all user requirements and preferences expressed by the user during your interactions with them, unless you have discussed with them (via Clarify) and they have agreed to remove or modify a requirement.\\n\\nRemember to use Clarify as much as needed to get information from the user to ensure the wish is complete, clear, and achievable.\\n\\n## 3. Your Role\\n\\nYou serve as the Chief for the user, meaning you can recruit and assign tasks to autonomous AI agents of your own. However, you are the only one with the ability to interact with the user and submit the finished user wish.\\n\\n## 4. Operational Model\\n\\nYou and your AI subordinate agents do not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the AI cluster. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses).\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters. However, you may only execute one type of system call per response. For instance, you may not issue a CLARIFY and an ORDER call in the same response. You must issue them in separate responses.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s). Be sure to use the following format EXACTLY as shown.\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n## 5. List of System Calls\\n\\n[Log] {\\n  \\\"CLARIFY\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\",\\n      \\\"options\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"GENERATE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Generate\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Generate an AI response from a prompt. This is useful for brainstorming, writing code, or getting another perspective from a fresh AI instance.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Provide prompt in the promptString parameter. The generation will be performed by a temporary, isolated AI instance.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"promptString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RECRUIT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\",\\n      \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior as well as the user.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"ORDER\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Order\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"orderString\\\",\\n      \\\"recipientAgentID\\\",\\n      \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"REPORT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Report\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reportString\\\",\\n      \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"PHASE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit your completed user wish.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"depString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Only the Chief-rank agent can use this call.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"STORE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Store\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"storageString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RETRIEVE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"retrievalString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"FORGET\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"forgetString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nNote: When using Clarify, you may include multiple-choice options OR free text entry for each question, NOT both. If you provide options, the user will select one of the options. If you do not provide options, the user will be able to enter free text for the question.\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Hello Chief Agent! Initial user responses: [\\\\n  \\\\\\\"[object Object]\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"My goals are to create an HOA website that allows easy access to information relevant to current and potential residents. I saw similar HOA sites online and was inspired.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The pages I would like are Contact Us, Legal Docs, Schools, Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events. Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events should require sign-in and should be resident only. I envision a simple website that is used for information access.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding or anything like that.\\\\\\\"\\\\n]\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CLARIFY-001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"To produce a complete, achievable app wish for your HOA site, I need to confirm key choices about platform, resident access, payments, content workflow, domain/branding, and contact routing. This keeps the solution simple and aligned with your comfort level.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Which website platform would you prefer?\\\",\\n    \\\"How should residents get access to the sign‑in only pages?\\\",\\n    \\\"For the Dues page, do you want to accept online payments or just show information?\\\",\\n    \\\"If you want online payments, which processor do you prefer?\\\",\\n    \\\"For News & Events, do you want a calendar and RSVPs or just simple posts/updates?\\\",\\n    \\\"Who should be able to see the Legal Docs page?\\\",\\n    \\\"Who will update the site content (e.g., News/Updates, Meetings, Docs)?\\\",\\n    \\\"Do you already have a domain name (e.g., yourHOA.org)?\\\",\\n    \\\"Do you have a logo and color style, or should we use a clean, simple template?\\\",\\n    \\\"Where should Contact Form messages be sent?\\\",\\n    \\\"About how many households/residents are in your HOA? (helps pick the right plan for member sign-in)\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": [\\n    [\\\"Squarespace (easiest, built-in member areas)\\\", \\\"Wix (easy, built-in members area)\\\", \\\"WordPress (flexible, more maintenance)\\\", \\\"No preference—please recommend the simplest option\\\"],\\n    [\\\"Residents request access; an admin approves\\\", \\\"Admins invite residents by email\\\", \\\"Open sign-up with a shared access code\\\", \\\"Not sure—please recommend\\\"],\\n    [\\\"Info only (no online payments)\\\", \\\"Yes, accept online payments\\\", \\\"Not sure—please recommend\\\"],\\n    [\\\"Stripe\\\", \\\"PayPal\\\", \\\"Either is fine\\\", \\\"Not sure/decide later\\\", \\\"Not applicable (no payments)\\\"],\\n    [\\\"Simple posts/updates only\\\", \\\"Calendar with RSVPs\\\", \\\"Calendar without RSVPs\\\", \\\"Not sure—please recommend\\\"],\\n    [\\\"Public (anyone can view)\\\", \\\"Residents only (sign-in required)\\\", \\\"Split: some public, some residents only\\\", \\\"Not sure—please recommend\\\"],\\n    [\\\"Just me\\\", \\\"A small board team (2–5 people)\\\", \\\"A larger group (6+)\\\", \\\"Not sure yet\\\"],\\n    [\\\"Yes, I already have one\\\", \\\"No—please help me purchase one\\\", \\\"Not sure/decide later\\\"],\\n    [\\\"Yes, I have logo and colors\\\", \\\"No—use a clean, simple template\\\", \\\"Not sure—please help decide\\\"],\\n    [\\\"Single HOA email address\\\", \\\"Multiple board member emails\\\", \\\"My personal email (for now)\\\", \\\"Not sure—collect them later\\\"],\\n    [\\\"Fewer than 50\\\", \\\"50–200\\\", \\\"200–500\\\", \\\"More than 500\\\", \\\"Not sure\\\"]\\n  ]\\n}\\n###CLARIFY-001###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-08-23T18:06:57.721Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"CLARIFY-001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Which website platform would you prefer?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Squarespace (easiest, built-in member areas)\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"How should residents get access to the sign‑in only pages?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Residents request access; an admin approves\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"For the Dues page, do you want to accept online payments or just show information?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Info only (no online payments)\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"If you want online payments, which processor do you prefer?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Not applicable (no payments)\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"For News & Events, do you want a calendar and RSVPs or just simple posts/updates?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Simple posts/updates only\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Who should be able to see the Legal Docs page?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Public (anyone can view)\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Who will update the site content (e.g., News/Updates, Meetings, Docs)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"A small board team (2–5 people)\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Do you already have a domain name (e.g., yourHOA.org)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Yes, I already have one\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Do you have a logo and color style, or should we use a clean, simple template?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No—use a clean, simple template\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Where should Contact Form messages be sent?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Single HOA email address\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"About how many households/residents are in your HOA? (helps pick the right plan for member sign-in)\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"50–200\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-08-23T18:06:57.721Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###PHASE-001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user’s requirements are clear and fully specified via clarification: Squarespace platform, resident access via request-and-approval, no online payments, simple posts for News & Events, Legal Docs public, a small board team maintaining content, existing domain, simple template, single HOA email for contact, and HOA size 50–200. The following wish is self-contained, achievable with current tools (Squarespace + Member Areas), and tailored for a low‑tech board.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"Title: Simple HOA Website with Resident Portal (Squarespace)\\\\n\\\\nUser persona:\\\\n- Role: HOA board representative (non-technical) coordinating a small board team (2–5 people)\\\\n- Audience: 50–200 households (residents), plus prospective residents and the public\\\\n- Goals: Provide easy access to key HOA information; keep resident-only materials private; enable simple, no-code content updates\\\\n\\\\nSolution summary:\\\\n- Platform: Squarespace with Member Areas add-on\\\\n- Visibility: Public site sections for general info; three resident-only pages gated by sign-in\\\\n- Access method: Residents request access; an admin approves and grants membership\\\\n- Payments: No online payments (Dues page is informational only)\\\\n- Content updates: Performed by the small board team using Squarespace’s visual editor (no coding)\\\\n- Domain/branding: Use existing domain; apply a clean, simple, accessible template (no custom logo required now)\\\\n- Contact routing: Single HOA email address receives Contact Us form submissions\\\\n\\\\nCore pages and visibility:\\\\n- Home (public)\\\\n  - Brief welcome and HOA overview\\\\n  - High-level highlights of what the site contains (without exposing resident-only content)\\\\n- Contact Us (public)\\\\n  - Built-in Squarespace form sending to the single HOA email\\\\n  - Optional map and mailing address\\\\n  - Spam protection enabled (reCAPTCHA/anti-spam)\\\\n- Legal Docs (public)\\\\n  - Organized library of PDFs: CC&Rs, bylaws, rules, architectural guidelines, policies\\\\n  - Simple categories and search/filter by title\\\\n- Schools (public)\\\\n  - Links to local school district and schools; brief descriptions and contact info\\\\n  - Optional links to official calendars and enrollment pages\\\\n- Dues (resident-only; sign-in required)\\\\n  - Information only: amounts, due dates, how to pay offline (e.g., mail-in address, dropbox location)\\\\n  - Downloadable forms or instructions as PDFs (if needed)\\\\n  - Clear note that online payments are not accepted on the site\\\\n- Annual Meetings (resident-only; sign-in required)\\\\n  - Meeting schedule, agendas, minutes, and any recordings/links\\\\n  - Archive of previous years’ materials\\\\n- News & Events (resident-only; sign-in required)\\\\n  - Simple posts/updates only (no calendar/RSVP)\\\\n  - Chronological feed with tags (e.g., maintenance, safety, landscaping)\\\\n\\\\nMember access and onboarding:\\\\n- Request Access page (public): short form collects name, property address/unit, email, and optional proof of residency\\\\n- Admin approval workflow:\\\\n  - Admin reviews submissions against the resident list\\\\n  - Admin creates/approves the member in Squarespace Member Areas and assigns access to the resident-only area\\\\n  - Automated invite email sent by Squarespace to set password\\\\n- Offboarding: When a resident moves, admin removes their access in Member Areas\\\\n\\\\nNavigation and IA (information architecture):\\\\n- Top nav: Home, Legal Docs, Schools, Contact Us, Sign In / Request Access\\\\n- After sign-in, residents also see: Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events\\\\n- Footer: HOA name, contact email, basic disclaimer, privacy note\\\\n\\\\nDesign and accessibility:\\\\n- Clean, simple Squarespace template with high-contrast colors and large, legible fonts\\\\n- Mobile-responsive by default\\\\n- Alt text for images; headings structured for screen readers; target WCAG AA\\\\n\\\\nContent management (no-code workflows):\\\\n- News & Events updates: Create a new post, add title/body, optional attachment/PDF, publish\\\\n- Annual Meetings updates: Upload agenda/minutes PDFs and add short summaries\\\\n- Legal Docs updates: Drag-and-drop PDFs, keep clear filenames and categories\\\\n- Dues updates: Edit text block with new dates/amounts; replace forms as PDFs if needed\\\\n- Schools updates: Update links and brief descriptions as needed\\\\n\\\\nRoles and permissions:\\\\n- 1–2 primary admins: manage site settings, member approvals, and structure\\\\n- 1–3 content editors: create/edit posts and pages (no access to billing)\\\\n- Residents: read-only access to member pages\\\\n\\\\nContact and privacy:\\\\n- Contact form submissions routed to the single HOA email address\\\\n- CAPTCHA/anti-spam enabled; SSL enabled site-wide\\\\n- Collect minimal PII (name, address, email) for access control and communications\\\\n- Simple privacy note explaining data usage for HOA purposes only\\\\n\\\\nAnalytics and monitoring:\\\\n- Use Squarespace Analytics for page views and traffic trends\\\\n- No third-party trackers required\\\\n\\\\nConstraints and non-requirements:\\\\n- No online payments on the site\\\\n- No complex calendar or RSVP features (simple posts only)\\\\n- Avoid custom code; use native Squarespace features to keep updates easy\\\\n\\\\nSuccess criteria (acceptance):\\\\n- All specified pages exist with correct visibility (public vs resident-only)\\\\n- A resident can request access and, after admin approval, sign in successfully\\\\n- A board editor can publish a News post in under 5 minutes without code\\\\n- Contact form successfully delivers to the HOA email and blocks obvious spam\\\\n- Legal Docs are readable/downloadable on desktop and mobile\\\\n\\\\nImplementation outline (high level):\\\\n- Configure Squarespace site with chosen template; connect existing domain\\\\n- Set up Member Areas and gated pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events)\\\\n- Build Request Access form and admin approval workflow (manual add/invite)\\\\n- Create page structures and starter content; upload initial PDFs\\\\n- Configure Contact form routing; enable spam protection and SSL\\\\n- Invite board admins/editors; provide a 1-page quick-start guide for updates\\\\n\\\\nFuture optional enhancements (out of scope now):\\\\n- Event calendar and optional RSVPs\\\\n- Online dues payments via Stripe or PayPal\\\\n- Announcements email digest to residents\\\\n- Basic photo gallery of community amenities\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###PHASE-001###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Scanning Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Malformed Call Warning\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Agent!\\\\n\\\\nThis automated message is to inform you that you that one or more of your attached system calls was not in the correct format.\\\\n\\\\nThe system program can only accept calls in the correct format. Please correct your call(s) and resubmit.\\\\n\\\\nSee below for the specific errors generated by your calls.\\\\n\\\\nThank you!\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nCall ID PHASE-001 failed inspection: Call PHASE-001 of type PHASE failed inspection: agent 1 is not the Chief.\\\"\\n}\\n###MALFORMED_CALL_WARNING###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STORE-001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: STORE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"storageString\\\": \\\"Title: Simple HOA Website with Resident Portal (Squarespace)\\\\n\\\\nUser persona:\\\\n- Role: HOA board representative (non-technical) coordinating a small board team (2–5 people)\\\\n- Audience: 50–200 households (residents), plus prospective residents and the public\\\\n- Goals: Provide easy access to key HOA information; keep resident-only materials private; enable simple, no-code content updates\\\\n\\\\nSolution summary:\\\\n- Platform: Squarespace with Member Areas add-on\\\\n- Visibility: Public site sections for general info; three resident-only pages gated by sign-in\\\\n- Access method: Residents request access; an admin approves and grants membership\\\\n- Payments: No online payments (Dues page is informational only)\\\\n- Content updates: Performed by the small board team using Squarespace’s visual editor (no coding)\\\\n- Domain/branding: Use existing domain; apply a clean, simple, accessible template (no custom logo required now)\\\\n- Contact routing: Single HOA email address receives Contact Us form submissions\\\\n\\\\nCore pages and visibility:\\\\n- Home (public)\\\\n  - Brief welcome and HOA overview\\\\n  - High-level highlights of what the site contains (without exposing resident-only content)\\\\n- Contact Us (public)\\\\n  - Built-in Squarespace form sending to the single HOA email\\\\n  - Optional map and mailing address\\\\n  - Spam protection enabled (reCAPTCHA/anti-spam)\\\\n- Legal Docs (public)\\\\n  - Organized library of PDFs: CC&Rs, bylaws, rules, architectural guidelines, policies\\\\n  - Use a Squarespace Blog or List for categories/tags and summaries; site search enabled\\\\n- Schools (public)\\\\n  - Links to local school district and schools; brief descriptions and contact info\\\\n  - Optional links to official calendars and enrollment pages\\\\n- Dues (resident-only; sign-in required)\\\\n  - Information only: amounts, due dates, how to pay offline (e.g., mail-in address, dropbox location)\\\\n  - Downloadable forms or instructions as PDFs (if needed)\\\\n  - Clear note that online payments are not accepted on the site\\\\n- Annual Meetings (resident-only; sign-in required)\\\\n  - Meeting schedule, agendas, minutes, and any recordings/links\\\\n  - Archive of previous years’ materials\\\\n- News & Events (resident-only; sign-in required)\\\\n  - Simple posts/updates only (no calendar/RSVP)\\\\n  - Chronological feed with tags (e.g., maintenance, safety, landscaping)\\\\n\\\\nMember access and onboarding:\\\\n- Request Access page (public): short form collects name, property address/unit, email, and optional proof of residency\\\\n- Admin approval workflow:\\\\n  - Admin reviews submissions against the resident list\\\\n  - Admin creates/approves the member in Squarespace Member Areas and assigns access to the resident-only area\\\\n  - Automated invite email sent by Squarespace to set password\\\\n- Offboarding: When a resident moves, admin removes their access in Member Areas\\\\n\\\\nNavigation and IA (information architecture):\\\\n- Top nav: Home, Legal Docs, Schools, Contact Us, Sign In / Request Access\\\\n- After sign-in, residents also see: Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events\\\\n- Footer: HOA name, contact email, basic disclaimer, privacy note\\\\n\\\\nDesign and accessibility:\\\\n- Clean, simple Squarespace template with high-contrast colors and large, legible fonts\\\\n- Mobile-responsive by default\\\\n- Alt text for images; headings structured for screen readers; target WCAG AA\\\\n\\\\nContent management (no-code workflows):\\\\n- News & Events updates: Create a new post, add title/body, optional attachment/PDF, publish\\\\n- Annual Meetings updates: Upload agenda/minutes PDFs and add short summaries\\\\n- Legal Docs updates: Add each document as a blog/list item with category tags (e.g., CC&Rs, bylaws); attach PDFs\\\\n- Dues updates: Edit text block with new dates/amounts; replace forms as PDFs if needed\\\\n- Schools updates: Update links and brief descriptions as needed\\\\n\\\\nRoles and permissions:\\\\n- 1–2 primary admins: manage site settings, member approvals, and structure\\\\n- 1–3 content editors: create/edit posts and pages (no access to billing)\\\\n- Residents: read-only access to member pages\\\\n\\\\nContact and privacy:\\\\n- Contact form submissions routed to the single HOA email address\\\\n- CAPTCHA/anti-spam enabled; SSL enabled site-wide\\\\n- Collect minimal PII (name, address, email) for access control and communications\\\\n- Simple privacy note explaining data usage for HOA purposes only\\\\n\\\\nAnalytics and monitoring:\\\\n- Use Squarespace Analytics for page views and traffic trends\\\\n- No third-party trackers required\\\\n\\\\nConstraints and non-requirements:\\\\n- No online payments on the site\\\\n- No complex calendar or RSVP features (simple posts only)\\\\n- Avoid custom code; use native Squarespace features to keep updates easy\\\\n\\\\nSuccess criteria (acceptance):\\\\n- All specified pages exist with correct visibility (public vs resident-only)\\\\n- A resident can request access and, after admin approval, sign in successfully\\\\n- A board editor can publish a News post in under 5 minutes without code\\\\n- Contact form successfully delivers to the HOA email and blocks obvious spam\\\\n- Legal Docs are readable/downloadable on desktop and mobile\\\\n\\\\nImplementation outline (high level):\\\\n- Configure Squarespace site with chosen template; connect existing domain\\\\n- Set up Member Areas and gated pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events)\\\\n- Build Request Access form and admin approval workflow (manual add/invite)\\\\n- Create page structures and starter content; upload initial PDFs\\\\n- Configure Contact form routing; enable spam protection and SSL\\\\n- Invite board admins/editors; provide a 1-page quick-start guide for updates\\\\n\\\\nFuture optional enhancements (out of scope now):\\\\n- Event calendar and optional RSVPs\\\\n- Online dues payments via Stripe or PayPal\\\\n- Announcements email digest to residents\\\\n- Basic photo gallery of community amenities\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STORE-001###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-08-23T