yments are not accepted\\n  - Annual Meetings: Schedule, agendas, minutes, and archives\\n  - News & Events: Simple posts/updates only (no calendar/RSVP), with tags for quick filtering\\n\\nResident access and approvals:\\n- Access request: Public “Request Access” page collects name, property address/unit, email, and optional proof of residency\\n- Admin workflow: An admin reviews requests, approves residents in Squarespace Member Areas, and triggers Squarespace’s invite email for password setup\\n- Offboarding: Admin removes access when residents move\\n\\nNavigation and visibility:\\n- Top navigation (public): Home, Legal Docs, Schools, Contact Us, Sign In / Request Access\\n- After sign-in (residents see): Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events\\n- Footer: HOA name, contact email, basic disclaimer, and privacy note\\n\\nContent management (no-code):\\n- News & Events: Create simple posts (title/body, optional PDF)\\n- Annual Meetings: Upload agendas/minutes as PDFs, add short summaries, maintain yearly archives\\n- Legal Docs: Upload PDFs with categories (e.g., CC&Rs, bylaws) for easy browsing\\n- Dues: Edit text for dates/amounts; replace PDFs as needed\\n- Schools: Update links and brief descriptions over time\\n\\nRoles and permissions:\\n- 1–2 primary admins: Site settings, member approvals, structure\\n- 1–3 content editors: Create/edit content only (no billing access)\\n- Residents: Read-only access to member pages\\n\\nDesign and accessibility:\\n- Simple, high-contrast, mobile-responsive template\\n- Clear headings, alt text, and legible fonts; target WCAG AA\\n\\nPrivacy and security:\\n- Contact form to single HOA email with CAPTCHA/anti-spam\\n- SSL enabled site-wide\\n- Minimal PII collection (name, address, email) solely for HOA communication and access control\\n- Simple privacy note explaining data use and retention\\n\\nAnalytics and monitoring:\\n- Use Squarespace Analytics to track traffic and page views\\n- No third-party trackers required initially\\n\\nConstraints and out-of-scope (for now):\\n- No online payments\\n- No calendar/RSVP features (posts only)\\n- Avoid custom code; prioritize native Squarespace features for ease of use\\n\\nSuccess criteria:\\n- All pages exist with correct visibility (public vs resident-only)\\n- A resident can request access, be approved by an admin, and sign in successfully\\n- A board editor can publish a News post in under 5 minutes without coding\\n- Contact form delivers messages to the HOA email and blocks obvious spam\\n- Legal documents are readable and downloadable on desktop and mobile\\n\\nHigh-level implementation plan:\\n- Choose a clean Squarespace template and connect the existing domain\\n- Enable Member Areas and configure gated pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events)\\n- Build the Request Access form and define the manual approval workflow\\n- Create initial page content and upload starter PDFs (docs, agendas/minutes)\\n- Set up Contact form routing and spam protection\\n- Invite admins/editors and provide a short quick-start guide for updates\\n\\nFuture optional enhancements:\\n- Add a calendar with optional RSVPs\\n- Enable online dues payments (Stripe or PayPal)\\n- Email digest for resident announcements\\n- Photo gallery of community amenities\\n\\nIf this matches your expectations, I can provide a one-page quick-start guide tailored to your board’s workflow in Squarespace next.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###BLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Scanning Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Blank Response Warning\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Agent!\\\\n\\\\nThis message is to inform you that you have issued a blank response (no system calls).\\\\n\\\\nYour response was heard by no one and no external effects occurred. This message is an automated system response, sent because you have not issued a system call in your response and you have no unresolved system calls.\\\\n\\\\nTo avo