entry for each question, NOT both. If you provide options, the user will select one of the options. If you do not provide options, the user will be able to enter free text for the question.\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Hello Chief Agent! Initial user responses: [\\\\n  \\\\\\\"[object Object]\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"My goals are to create an HOA website that allows easy access to information relevant to current and potential residents. I saw similar HOA sites online and was inspired.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The pages I would like are Contact Us, Legal Docs, Schools, Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events. Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events should require sign-in and should be resident only. I envision a simple website that is used for information access.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding or anything like that.\\\\\\\"\\\\n]\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CLARIFY-001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"To produce a complete, achievable app wish for your HOA site, I need to confirm key c